## Use the TypedResults API

Returning <xref:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.TypedResults> rather than <xref:Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http.Results> has several advantages, including testability and automatically returning the response type metadata for OpenAPI to describe the endpoint. For more information, see `TypedResults` versus `Results`.

The `Map<HttpVerb>` methods can call route handler methods instead of using lambdas. To see an example, update *Program.cs* with the following code:

